WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.440
Is this friendship an abomination&nbsp;
in the eyes of the law? Or can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.800
a sorcerer supreme and a reformed&nbsp;
supervillain find genuine connection?

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:14.040
"She-Hulk: Attorney at Law" wastes no time in&nbsp;
utilizing the vast powerhouse that is the Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:19.260
Cinematic Universe. Throughout the nine-episode&nbsp;
series, "She-Hulk" brings in several characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.960
and references from the MCU, placing them directly&nbsp;
in the path of the fourth-wall breaking Jennifer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.640
Walters. After the first episode explored&nbsp;
the relationship between Jen and her cousin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.200
Bruce Banner, fans got a chance to see&nbsp;
Sorcerer Supreme Wong, Emil Blonsky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:40.020
Daredevil, and even several references to New&nbsp;
Asgard, Thor, and the love life of Captain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.060
America. In other words, "She-Hulk" is acutely&nbsp;
aware of its position in a greater narrative.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:49.260
With the finale of "She-Hulk," several new&nbsp;
elements have been introduced that could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.940
be laying the groundwork for future&nbsp;
MCU movies and TV series. Perhaps the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.780
greatest shocker in "She-Hulk," though,&nbsp;
is the introduction of Hulk's son Skaar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.340
which some fans believe may be setting&nbsp;
up a "World War Hulk" movie. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:06.180
in the Marvel tradition, the finale&nbsp;
features a post-credit scene which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.140
raises particular questions about the&nbsp;
future of some fan-favorite characters.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:15.720
Although "She-Hulk: Attorney at Law" sets up&nbsp;
a battle among She-Hulk, Hulk, Abomination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:21.900
a transformed Todd Phelps, and Titania, She-Hulk&nbsp;
uses her ability to break the fourth wall and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:27.240
enters into our reality, where she demands to&nbsp;
see "Kevin," which is a direct call-out to Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:32.880
Studios honcho Kevin Feige. After finding out&nbsp;
that Kevin is actually an artificial intelligence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.740
she calls for changes that will hold people&nbsp;
accountable for their actions. This causes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:43.920
brewing epic battle to be completely tossed out,&nbsp;
and instead both Todd and Emil are arrested — Todd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.180
for hacking Jen's computer and phone, and&nbsp;
Emil for breaking the terms of his parole.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.620
Considering Emil Blonsky's new outlook&nbsp;
on life and general Zen demeanor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:57.420
he accepts his responsibility and his&nbsp;
punishment of 10 years in prison. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:00.960
the end credits stinger in the&nbsp;
"She-Hulk" finale shows Wong once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.860
again using his sling-ring to open&nbsp;
a portal into Emil's glass prison.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:10.560
One reason for Wong's continuing efforts to break&nbsp;
Emil Blonsky out of prison could be that Wong and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:15.180
Blonsky are actually friends. In the third&nbsp;
episode, Wong appears on behalf of Blonsky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:19.680
during his parole hearing. The authorities&nbsp;
want to know why and how Blonsky escaped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.240
and Wong explains that he did it, and even&nbsp;
though Wong offered Blonsky sanctuary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:28.740
Blonsky turned this offer down in order&nbsp;
to show that he's reformed. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:33.801
the authorities point out that Wong committed&nbsp;
a crime by letting Blonsky go free for a time

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:40.140
"You realize that you've just admitted to&nbsp;
facilitating a prisoner escape which is a crime?"

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:41.159
"I must go."

00:02:41.798 --> 00:02:47.280
Wong may consider Emil Blonsky an actual friend,&nbsp;
and since Blonsky is only being sent back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.960
prison for a parole violation, Wong couldn't&nbsp;
let him lose a decade of his life. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:55.500
there could be another reason why&nbsp;
Wong decided to spring Blonsky again.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:03:00.540
Prior to "She-Hulk," the Abomination's&nbsp;
last MCU appearance came with a cameo in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:04.740
"Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings."&nbsp;
As "She-Hulk" reveals, that movie's cage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:10.020
fight between Wong and Abomination was part of&nbsp;
Wong's training. Wong required a worthy foe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:14.400
and Abomination happened to fit the bill.&nbsp;
There's no animosity between the two,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.980
as highlighted by "She-Hulk" and its finale scene,&nbsp;
so it could be that Wong is simply thankful for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:24.840
Emil's efforts in this department, or it could be&nbsp;
that Wong has the intention of using Abomination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:30.343
in the training of other students. He could also&nbsp;
be making good on his original offer of sanctuary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:34.980
because it's probably hard to get somebody&nbsp;
extradited from Kamar-Taj. Or perhaps there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.993
even a chance for a future TV show centered&nbsp;
on Wong and his who's who of superfriends.

00:03:39.993 --> 00:03:42.360
For his part, Benedict Wong has made it clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.738
he loves playing the character.&nbsp;
He told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:03:45.738 --> 00:03:49.920
"I'm just enjoying playing this role and&nbsp;
where it takes me. In every single kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.360
project that they invite me to be involved in,&nbsp;
it just pulls away another layer of the onion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:59.531
you know? You get to find a little bit more about&nbsp;
the eccentricities of the Sorcerer Supreme."

00:03:59.531 --> 00:04:02.760
Now Marvel fans just need&nbsp;
to sit back, breathe deep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.098
and await the next appearance of the&nbsp;
Abomination and the Sorcerer Supreme.

